From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 10:14:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Catch IMS download failures instead of crashing the app

The treble.phh.me SSL certificate expired, causing DownloadManager to
throw an exception during IMS APK download. The unhandled exception
kills the Treble app process.

Wrap dm!!.enqueue() in a try/catch and show a Toast with the error
message so the user knows what happened instead of experiencing a
sudden crash.

Issue: #66
---
 app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/ImsSettings.kt | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/ImsSettings.kt b/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/ImsSettings.kt
index 8a30a77..37d87b7 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/ImsSettings.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/me/phh/treble/app/ImsSettings.kt
@@ -143,7 +143,13 @@ class ImsSettingsFragment : SettingsFragment() {
 
             downloadRequest.setDestinationInExternalFilesDir(activity, Environment.DIRECTORY_DOWNLOADS, "ims.apk")
 
-            val myId = dm!!.enqueue(downloadRequest)
+            val myId: Long
+            try {
+                myId = dm!!.enqueue(downloadRequest)
+            } catch (e: Exception) {
+                Toast.makeText(activity, "IMS download failed: " + e.message, Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show()
+                return@setOnPreferenceClickListener true
+            }
 
             activity.registerReceiver(object: BroadcastReceiver() {
                 override fun onReceive(context: Context, intent: Intent) {
-- 
